# Stingerquill Charm's second mode: "Target creature gains first strike and deathtouch until end of turn." Bot1's
# Ornithopter has both while the turn lasts (checked in the main phase) and neither on turn 3, when the effect has ended
# (CR 514.2); the mode targets a creature only, so Bot2 as a target is refused beside the creature as the control.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Jet
Mox Ruby
Stingerquill Charm
Ornithopter
Mountain x20

[Bot2 Deck]
Forest x14

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Stingerquill Charm.Cast
Bot1.Modes(2)
! Bot1.Target(Bot2)
Bot1.Target(Ornithopter)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
? Bot1.Battlefield.Ornithopter.Keywords = Deathtouch; FirstStrike; Flying
[T3 Bot1.Main1]

[Expect]
Bot1.Battlefield.Ornithopter.Keywords = Flying
Bot1.Graveyard = Stingerquill Charm
